==English==

===Etymology===
A calque of {{etyl|es|en}} {{term|momento de la verdad|el momento de la verdad|lang=es}}, which refers to the time of the final sword thrust in a [[bullfight]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[moment]] [[of]] [[truth]]|moments of truth}}

# {{idiomatic}} A deciding instant; the time when a [[test]] determines or makes it apparent whether something will succeed.
#: ''The '''moment of truth''' comes when you try to start the engine you have just rebuilt.''

